\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qc\sl240\slmult1{\b\ul\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 The
 Ultrasonic Transducer Transmitter and Receiver\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qc\sl240\slmult1{\b\ul\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28\par
}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1{\b\ul\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 To My
 Valued Customers:\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 I\u8217\'92
d like to take a second before I start to say thank you to all that chose to shop
 at  the HobbyTronixStore.  It is a small business that I run on the side, and it
\u8217\'92s good to know that in these poor economic times, there are still people
 out there who share the same interest and passion towards electronics that I have
.  Thanks to all of you.  I hope you find this document useful.\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1{\b\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1{\b\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 Sincerely
,\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1{\b\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 Patrick
 Mitchell\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1{\b\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 Electronics
 Engineering Technician\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1{\b\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 HobbyTronixStore
 - {\ul\cf1{{\field{\*\fldinst{ HYPERLINK "http://www.electroniclessons.com/"}}{
\fldrslt{\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1 www.electroniclessons.com}}}
}}\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qc\sl240\slmult1{\b\ul\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28\par
}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\qc\sl240\slmult1{\b\ul\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 LET
\u8217\'92S GET STARTED!\par}

\pard\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\sl240\slmult1{\f0\lang1033\fs20\kerning28 Okay!  So
 in every electronic circuit, there must be a power supply, correct?  Well in this
 care we\u8217\'92re going to need three different supplies.  Don\u8217\'92t worry
, you\u8217\'92re not going to really need three different sources of power.  Only
 two.  First of all, we\u8217\'92re going to construct our power supply for the 
ultrasonic transmitter circuit.  As you can see below, all we need is a 9v battery
/connector (Fully charged battery), and two capacitors.  Now, if you\u8217\'92re
 using a battery, you don\u8217\'92t necessarily need the two capacitors. It\u8217
\'92s just good practice to implement them.  If you\u8217\'92re using another source
 of power; perhaps an AC to DC wall transformer, which I don\u8217\'92t suggest 
you do, then the capacitors are a very good idea.  I greatly advise that you use
 batteries for this project..  That being said, the power supply circuit is really
 up to you. You can customize it, and go all out with protection and what not.  
However, if you\u8217\'92re taking my advice, and using a 9v battery, I wouldn\u8217
\'92t worry too much about noise effecting the performance.  We have to worry more
 about noise at the receiver than we do at the transmitter, so don\u8217\'92t waste
 too much time worrying about it.  I don\u8217\'92t suggest using a power supply
 larger than 9VDC.  If you decide to use a wall transformer, I suggest actually 
testing the output value with a multi-meter before using it.  I\u8217\'92ve found
 several wall transformers that are rated to output 9VDC, and actually output 12
-15VDC, so beware.\par}

