 not necessary if you\u8217\'92re using a 9v battery, as batteries are primarily
 stable.  We want to connect the positive lead of our 9v battery to pin#3 of a 78L05
 5v regulator.  If you decide to use an LM7805 regulator instead, make sure you 
google the data sheet, as the pin-out is reversed. We want to connect the negative
 lead of our battery to the middle pin of the 78L05 as well.  Pin#1 should then 
read 5VDC.  Make sure you check for 5v at pin#1 using a multi-meter once you\u8217
\'92ve made all your power supply connections.  This 5VDC line will be our circuit
 VCC. \par}

